Track identity: **Track A (USD)** = `hal-deep`/red family; **Track B (ITESM)** = `navy`/steel family; **Kuwait** callouts = green.

## 4. Chart grammar (from native chart XML of Data Centers / KLA / Mitsubishi / FEMSA)

* **Bar/column charts: no gridlines, value axis deleted** (12 of 12 stacked/clustered bar charts measured) — values live on data labels. **Line/scatter charts** keep a value axis (9–10 pt) and may use light gridlines (9 of 35 charts). Category axis: baseline line only (black 1 pt), labels 9–12 pt (9 pt is the mode).
* Column charts: `gapWidth` **80** (mode; range 60–120), stacked `overlap` **100**, clustered `overlap` **−27**. Bars with solid fill, **no outlines, no 3-D, no shadow**.
* Data labels: 9–11 pt (9 pt mode); inside white on dark segments, outside black above bars; **totals as bold labels above stacks** (hidden scatter/line series trick = "Total Capex" series with `dLblPos = t`).
* Lines: 2.25 pt (28575 EMU) with no markers; average/target as red dashed (#F21C27) line.
* Legend: **bottom**, 9–12 pt, no border. Single series → no legend.
* Header block above each chart: 16 pt bold + 1 pt black rule + 12 pt *italic* unit/description ("Amounts in USD millions"). Source goes in the slide source line, not under the chart.
* **Forecast zone**: light-grey (#F2F2F2, dotted pattern in Aztlan) rectangle behind estimate years + italic label "Consensus Forecast"; estimates in lighter tint; years suffixed `E`.
* Callouts: oval "CAGR x.x%" bubble between first/last bar; dashed average line; waterfall with green (+)/red (−)/navy (total) bars.
* Pie/donut: only for 2–4 slices, labels with %, hollow center for the key number.
* Heat-map tables (sensitivity): red→yellow→green fill scale, highlighted base case with bordered cell (Ingevity s34, FEMSA s17).
* Bloomberg/Yahoo **dark-theme screenshots are NOT pasted as charts** (they break the white system). Rebuild from data (CSV in `08_Assets/data`) in house style; use the original screenshot only as an "evidence" thumbnail with source in footer.

## 5. Table grammar (COM-measured)

* Header row: fill `#242852` (Aztlan) → **HAL: `hal-deep` #8B1318**, white bold 11 pt, centered; first column left.
* Body: 11 pt, white / `#F2F2F2` zebra, numbers right-aligned, negatives in parentheses or red; **peer-median row bold on light fill**; subject-company row highlighted in light blue (Aztlan uses #C2D7F6 / #F2F2F2) → HAL: `#EAD2D2` (rose tint).
* Borders: thin black rules top/bottom of table and under header only; no vertical borders (FEMSA table: thin gray horizontals).
* Row height **0.32–0.36 in** for presentation tables (KLA s4/s10/s13 measured 0.325–0.355), **0.19–0.29 in** for financial-statement appendix tables (30 rows × 12 cols at 8–9 pt); actual columns white, estimate columns light-blue/yellow tint with a bold green "CAGR" band.
* Always a left "Metric" column; units in the header (`$ in millions`).

## 6. Component library (shapes found repeatedly)

* **Colored header boxes** (3–5 across): rectangle with bold white 12–14 pt text, 0.3–0.4 in high, fill = series color; below each a white box with thin outline and 10–11 pt bullets (KLA s3, Mitsubishi s11).
* **Chevron/process chain** with a red dashed bracket for "where we focus" (KLA s7).
* **Parallelogram section tags** (FEMSA s3), **roman-numeral agenda pills** (FEMSA s2: pill #9B2C39 + light-grey bar #F2F2F2, Helvetica 14).
* **Dashed-outline bullet boxes** (GTT s22) for "evidence by region".
* **"So what / Key takeaway" strip**: 12 pt bold in a `#F2F2F2` rounded box, thin top rule (Data Centers s4–s7 "Key Takeaways" column, FEMSA bottom bullets).
* Logos: 0.5–0.9 in high, always on white, aligned to a box; company logo at top-right of the *content* when profiling that company (KLA s3, Mitsubishi s3).
* Pictures (company photos) get **no border**, cropped to the box, 0.1 in minimum gap to text; max 1–2 per slide.

## 7. Slide-type catalogue (what exists / what does NOT)

Standard sequence in the user's decks: **Cover → (Disclaimer) → Company overview → Quant/Model (skip) → Investment call → Key topics (3–6 slides, each = claim title + chart/diagram + bullets) → Market/Competition → Financials (appendix: IS, ratios, valuation, CF, BS, WACC, DCF, sensitivity) → Closing**. Section divider = full-color slide with giant title (GTT s8/s19/s25).

What the templates **do not** use (so do not add it): clip-art, stock icons in color boxes (except think-cell icon sets), 3-D effects, shadows, gradients on shapes, drop caps, more than 2 fonts, emojis, animated builds, text below 9 pt in body, centered paragraphs, colored backgrounds on content slides (only cover/divider/closing), headline without a verb ("Revenue" ≠ "Revenue grew 12% on…"). Titles are **action sentences** (≤ 70 chars, one line at 28 pt over 9.8 in ≈ 62 chars) with the subtitle carrying the quantified so-what.

